WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:08.750
Understand the builder sentence: show me a measure using a calculation, grouped by dimensions.

00:08.750 --> 00:17.500
Choose the measure: the business value you want to analyse, such as value in billions of US dollars.

00:17.500 --> 00:26.250
Choose the aggregation. Sum adds matching values; Average, Count, Minimum and Maximum answer different questions.

00:26.250 --> 00:35.000
Add the first dimension. Flow direction splits the total into Import and Export series.

00:35.000 --> 00:43.750
Add a second dimension. Period label creates a nested comparison without replacing flow direction.

00:43.750 --> 00:52.500
Filter the records, sort the result and set a limit to focus the business question.

00:52.500 --> 01:01.250
Choose a suitable visual and enable labels when exact values matter.

01:01.250 --> 01:10.000
Give the visual a meaningful title, choose a dashboard and pin it. The title remains when the visual is edited later.
